# Copy to the collector stack's .env. REVIEW TEMPLATE, not deployed.
# Use only AFTER ADR 0027 item 14 is proven (docs/deployment/collector.md).
# Image: must be a release that contains `archive job` (not yet released).
COGVAULT_VERSION=
NAS_UID=1026
NAS_GID=100
COGVAULT_DIR=/volume1/docker/cogvault
# Archive registry root on the NAS LOCAL disk (never SMB), owned by
# NAS_UID:NAS_GID. Deliberately EMPTY: do not assume a path.
# /volume1/docker/cogvault/archive already exists and holds manual bundles. It
# is not known to be an empty directory or a cogvault registry root, so do not
# point ARCHIVE_DIR at it until the operator has inventoried it (see
# docs/deployment/collector.md, "Choosing the archive root").
ARCHIVE_DIR=
# Directory on the NAS host through which the ADR 0027 item 14 evidence is
# reachable. Deliberately EMPTY: its location is a deployment decision (it is
# where the off-NAS backup target, report, and replica are visible). It must
# already contain backups/, reports/ (holding restore-test.json) and replica/
# (holding deletions-log.jsonl), so Docker does not create root-owned
# directories. The long-running containers mount only reports/ and replica/,
# read-only, at /evidence/reports and /evidence/replica.
EVIDENCE_DIR=
